            <ArticleTitle>Occipital nerve block in the management of headache and cervical pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The origins of chronic headache and the role of the greater occipital nerve in headache syndromes are reviewed. The anatomical pathways and physiological basis of these headaches are discussed with a view to synthesizing some current concepts of headache generation. Studies of occipital nerve blockade for treatment of headaches of various types are assessed and a retrospective analysis of our own experience is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
